  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "This paper proposes QEKLR, a hybrid gate-based quantum-classical classifier using ZZFeatureMap and a fidelity quantum kernel with logistic regression. It reports 100% accuracy on the synthetic dataset and Iris subset, 92.31% accuracy on Statlog Heart Disease with 2 features, and 94.87% accuracy with 4 features (MCC 0.88, AUC-ROC 0.98), but the strongest classical baselines match or closely track these results, so no practical quantum advantage is demonstrated.",
